    "categoryEn": "Betrothal & Customary Oath",
    "descriptionEn": "Manyiriah and Batimbang Tando constitute the sacred customary betrothal and engagement ceremony in the Minangkabau matrilineal kinship system. The prospective bride's family sends customary delegates to the prospective groom's family carrying ceremonial betel pouches.\n\nThis is followed by Batimbang Tando (exchanging heirloom pledges), where both families exchange valued heirlooms such as gold-embossed keris daggers, antique songket fabrics, or ancestral jewelry before clan elders and religious leaders.\n\nThis tradition honors democratic consensus, eloquent customary rhetoric (petatah-petitih), and formalizes the enduring alliance between two matrilineal clans.",
