    "descriptionEn": "Randai is a traditional Minangkabau folk theater performance that brilliantly integrates various art forms, including martial arts (silek), dance, drama, vocal chanting (dendang), and music. In the performance, dozens of actors stand in a large circle, stepping dynamically while slapping their baggy traditional trousers, creating an iconic, rhythmic clapping sound.\n\nDialogues in Randai are not simply spoken; they are chanted or sung in rhythmic poems (gurindam) telling local folktales (kaba). The stories typically revolve around heroic legends or classic Minangkabau romances, such as Malin Kundang, Sabai nan Aluih, or Cindua Mato.\n\nThis communal art form serves as a central gathering event in open village squares at night. Randai is heavily laden with moral lessons and customary proverbs, entertainingly imparted to the younger generation.",
