    "id": "cu19",
    "descriptionEn": "Bareh Randang is an exquisite traditional sweet delicacy from Payakumbuh and Lima Puluh Kota Regency holding ceremonial status in Minangkabau matrimonial gift exchanges (manjalang). 'Bareh' means glutinous rice, while 'randang' refers to dry-roasting over direct heat.\n\nSelected white glutinous rice is dry-roasted with aromatic pandan leaves, finely ground, and kneaded into a rich syrup of boiled palm sugar and thick coconut milk. The dough is pressed into wooden frames and sliced into square confections.\n\nBareh Randang offers a distinctive toasted rice aroma, deep caramelized palm sugar sweetness, and a dense, velvety yet pleasantly crumbly texture that melts delightfully on the palate.",
    "originEn": "Payakumbuh & Lima Puluh Kota Regency",
