    "type": "Kudapan Khas",
    "descriptionEn": "Kue Bika Koto Baru is a beloved mountain cake baked at roadside stalls along the chilly mountain pass of Koto Baru between Padang Panjang and Bukittinggi, nestled beneath Mount Singgalang and Marapi.\n\nThe batter combines rice flour, freshly grated young coconut, coconut water, and palm sugar (red bika) or cane sugar (white bika). Spooned into clay molds lined with banana or teak leaves, it is baked using the traditional 'Two-Fires' method—charcoal glowing underneath and burning on the iron lid above.\n\nThe exterior forms a lightly charred, smoky crust from teak leaves while the interior remains pillowy soft, delightfully chewy, and rich with warm young coconut sweetness."
