    "flavorProfileEn": "Tender meaty texture, rich spiced red coconut curry broth, warming spicy depth",
    "descriptionEn": "Gulai Jariang is an authentic highland Minangkabau curry elevating jengkol beans (Archidendron pauciflorum) into a deeply cherished culinary delicacy with a tender, meaty texture.\n\nMature jengkol beans are boiled with guava leaves to mellow their pungent aroma, then gently crushed (ditokok) so the beans flatten and open up. They are slow-cooked in thick coconut curry broth spiced with turmeric, chilies, lemongrass, galangal, kaffir lime leaves, and asam kandis.\n\nThe spiced coconut gravy deeply infuses the tender beans, yielding a rich, buttery, savory texture beloved across the Minangkabau homeland.",
