    "descriptionEn": "Rendang Lokan is a legendary coastal rendang variation indigenous to Pesisir Selatan Regency, substituting beef with fresh wild estuary clams (lokan) harvested from brackish river deltas. Coastal Minangkabau communities along the Inderapura and Batang Tarusan estuaries have prepared clam rendang for centuries, showcasing ancestral mastery over marine foraging.\n\nFresh clams retrieved from riverbed mud are meticulously purged and cleaned, then slowly braised with pure coconut milk and the complete repertoire of Minang rendang aromatics: crushed chilies, ginger, galangal, lemongrass, turmeric leaves, and asam kandis. The reduction is coaxed over hours until the coconut fats caramelize into rich dark-brown spice crumbles coating each succulent clam.\n\nThe chewy, savory-sweet texture of coastal clams marries flawlessly with the fiery, umami-laden rendang spices and smoky firewood aroma. Rendang Lokan has become a sought-after culinary souvenir among food connoisseurs seeking West Sumatra's marine heritage.",
